  "card": "Adds destructors to CHMAC_SHA256 and CHMAC_SHA512 to cleanse inner and outer hasher states and switches MuSig2 partial signing keypair storage to secure memory. Without this, destroyed HMAC instances retain HMAC output and final message blocks in memory, leaving behind seeds from CExtKey::SetSeed() and parent private keys from hardened BIP32 operations, while MuSig2 leaves secret keys on the stack. The author confirmed with a test program that key and seed bytes persist after Finalize() and are zeroed by the new destructors.",
